course: dictionary
lesson: 6613
title: Going north
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: North is one of the four main directions. The other three are south, east and west. On most maps, north is at the top, so find north first and the other directions fall into place.
explain: Look at the words around north to work out its meaning. «Corsica, just north of it, belongs to France.» The words «just north of» tell you where Corsica lies compared with the island it is next to.
explain: North can also be a direction of travel. «We drove north» means we travelled towards the top of the map. Here north is a word that tells us how we moved.
explain: North can name a place too. «The north side of a hill» is the side that faces north, so north is a part of the hill, not a movement.
fact: North is one of the four main directions: north, south, east and west.
fact: On most maps, north is at the top.
fact: «The North Pole» is the most northern point of the Earth.
fact: At midday in Britain the Sun is in the south, so «shadows point north».
fact: A compass needle points north.
exercise: «We drove north» for hours. What does north mean in this sentence? | Slowly and quietly | Backwards to where we started | *Towards the top of the map | Towards the sea and the sand
exercise: At midday in Britain the Sun is in the south. Which way do the shadows point? | East | *North | West | South
exercise: «Corsica, just north of it, belongs to France.» What does north of mean here? | Far away across the sea in the south | *In the direction of the north, a little way from | Inside the same island | Below it on the map
test: Which of the four main directions is at the top of most maps? | East | *North | West | South
test: The North Pole is the most ____ point of the Earth. | western | southern | *northern | eastern
exam: In «We drove north», what kind of word is north? | *An adverb, a word that tells us the direction | A verb, a doing word | A noun, a name for a place | An adjective, a describing word
